Graded view: PC Grade and CL Grade columns; prices compared only on the same grade

- Each row now carries PriceCharting's own grade and Card Ladder's own grade (graded_site.pc_grade / cl_grade).
  CL Grade is Card Ladder's label on the card's page; PC Grade is the grade PriceCharting's price is for. Its
  Grade 9 / 8 / 7 / 9.5 chart lines blend every grader, so such a row says "Grade 9 (any grader)", not PSA 9.
- The Grade column is now PC Grade, with CL Grade beside it (saved layouts keep their order). Both turn red when
  they differ, and PC to CL % then says "≠ grade" instead of comparing two different grades' prices.
- Review: each side shows its own grade; the Card Ladder picture is only ever a slab of this row's grade (no
  fallback to the page's main picture), and it opens full size.
- The build log counts the rows whose two grades differ.

